## 🧭 NOTE — Proposed Stable Plan: Design & Deployment (OPEN for later deliberation)

Recorded so the **decision-making process can be revisited and designs re-evaluated
"when the time is right"** — a decision trail, not a locked plan. Mirror in
`tasks/todo.md` → "Proposed Stable Plan — Design & Deployment."

**Design system**
- ✅ Styling base: **Tailwind CSS** (approved).
- 🟡 **Component library — OPEN**: the doc-recommended default is **shadcn/ui (Radix)**,
  but the user is **strongly considering Lightswind UI or MeetUI** (in addition to /
  instead of solely shadcn + Radix) — see "Component Library Options" note below.
  Evaluate licensing/cost, accessibility, React 18 + Next.js App Router fit, theming/
  dark mode, bundle size, maintenance velocity, and copy-&-modify-ability before deciding.
- 🎨 Ideal: a component library we can *modify* and *own*, inspired by Vercel-style
  reference templates — not a heavy, opinionated, purchased template.

**Deployment**
- 🟡 Model (settled direction): **Dockerized standalone Next.js modular monolith**
  (web + API + PostgreSQL + Redis + worker). **NOT** WordPress / not a plugin (non-goal).
- 🟡 **Host — OPEN**: VPS (DigitalOcean) / Fly.io / Railway / Render / TBD. The
  background worker + durable queue + DB favour a **container-capable host** over
  serverless-only; Vercel = frontend inspiration, not sole hosting for this stack.
- ⏳ Deferred: self-hosting branding, white-label, mobile, K8s/microservices (Stage 4+).

**Animation**
- 🎞 CSS transitions first; **anime.js** (or Framer Motion) deferred until concrete
  animation requirements exist. anime.js is framework-agnostic and non-conflicting,
  so it can be added later without rework.

**Next:** formalize as ADRs (`deployment platform`, `design-system foundation`) once the
component library and host are chosen; do a design/tech-eval pass before frontend build-out.

